# THE ASSURANCE REPORT IS BUILT, NEVER COMMITTED.
#
# It is a few MB of generated HTML per run, it embeds the fonts and the logo on
# every page, and it would produce an enormous diff on every build for content
# that is fully reproducible from `python quality/run_assurance.py`. Committing it
# would also freeze a verdict in the tree that stops matching the data the moment
# the corpus is rebuilt.
#
# The profile BASELINE (quality/baseline/) is the opposite and IS committed — it
# is the reference the next run diffs against, so it has to travel with the repo.
quality/out/
quality/gx/uncommitted/

# Full finding write-ups belong in the PRIVATE hackathon-organisers repo.
# This repository is public; open bug reports about data we are about to hand
# to participants are not. The public half is quality/known-findings.yml.
quality/FINDINGS.md
quality/FINDINGS.for-organisers-repo.md
